# ── Accepted: reachability CVEs that this deployment's isolation neutralises ──
#
# Kagetora runs on the crunchtools-kagetora Podman network: internal=true,
# dns_enabled=false, nothing published to the host, and exactly two containers
# on it (kagetora and mcp-trentina). Every CVE below requires an attacker to
# CONNECT to this container. Nothing can, short of already owning Trentina.
#
# MCP Python SDK 1.26.0 -> 1.27.2/1.28.1. All three are server-transport bugs:
# HTTP transport session handling, experimental task handlers accepting any
# client, WebSocket server transport. Cannot be fixed in place -- hermes-agent
# 0.19.0 pins mcp==1.26.0 and is written against the 1.x client API; forcing it
# resolves to mcp 2.1.1 and breaks the import Kagetora needs (verified by a
# build-time smoke test, not assumed). Upstream fixes this properly in 0.21.0,
# which ships mcp 2.0.0.
CVE-2026-52869
CVE-2026-52870
CVE-2026-59950
#
# Starlette 1.0.1 -> 1.1.0/1.3.1. Also server-side: SSRF via UNC paths in
# StaticFiles, and form limits being ignored (DoS). The SSRF is doubly dead
# here -- SSRF needs somewhere to send the request and this container has no
# egress at all. Fixed upstream in 0.21.0 (starlette 1.3.1).
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283
#
# PyJWT 2.12.1 -> 2.13.0, auth bypass via forged JWTs. The most serious in
# class, and the one that would matter first if the network boundary ever
# slipped -- but it still requires reaching the socket. Fixed upstream in
# 0.21.0 (PyJWT 2.13.0). Worth revisiting the moment 0.21 becomes reachable.
CVE-2026-48526

# ── Accepted: pip's own vendored bundle, not packages Hermes imports ──
#
#   GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack     OOB read on Unpacker reuse
#   CVE-2025-47273       setuptools  path traversal in PackageIndex
#
# These live in site-packages/pip/_vendor/ (confirmed by reading the built
# image: the vendored msgpack/__init__.py declares version (1, 1, 2), with
# pkg_resources beside it). Trivy files them under its aggregate "Python"
# target with no path in the report summary and no "(METADATA)" marker -- that
# missing marker is the tell, and chasing it cost three wrong theories.
#
# Not fixable: the versions are frozen inside pip. Removing pip is unsafe
# because Hermes lazy-installs skill dependencies at runtime. Both are only
# reachable through pip's own index traffic, which this container cannot
# originate.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# NOTE: Pillow is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the one finding this
# deployment's isolation does not cover -- Matrix delivers internet-originated
# images into a vision-enabled agent and Pillow parses them -- so it is patched
# forward in the Containerfile instead.
